.TH GENESIS-ARCADE 7 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-arcade \- the games in Genesis's outer world: official ARC-AGI-3
and the Kaggle Game Arena shelf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgames.arcade.Arcade\fR      the place itself, attached to OuterEnvironment
\fBgames.official\fR           the official ARC-AGI-3 doorway (arc_agi)
\fBgames.arena\fR              the local arena shelf (pyspiel) + CombinedGames
\fBarcade_*\fR                        her tools for it (see \fBgenesis-cli\fR(1), \fB/arcade\fR)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a video game. It is not real and it is just for fun; she is
safe. The arcade is part of her outer world, not her mind: it offers
games, she chooses whether to play, and every board reaches her
through
.B OuterEnvironment.perceive
while every move returns through
.BR OuterEnvironment.it_acted
\(em memory, cognition, emotion, learning, brain waves, neurochemistry
and telemetry arrive by the same paths as the rest of her world. The
directions she is given
.RI ( Outer_World/games/DIRECTIONS.md )
say she cannot know the instructions: she must explore, remember, and
solve, carrying what each level teaches to the next.
.PP
One arcade, two catalogues: \fBCombinedGames\fR merges them so the
offer list covers both shelves and \fBarena:\fR-prefixed ids route to
the arena while bare ids route to the official API.
.SH SHELVES
.SS Official ARC-AGI-3 \(em games.official
The doorway to the official interactive-environments service
( https://three.arcprize.org ) through the \fBarc_agi\fR toolkit
(\fBArcade\fR, \fBOperationMode\fR) and its \fBarcengine\fR. The mode
comes from \fB$GENESIS_ARC_MODE\fR:
.TP
.B normal
(default) download each game once into \fI<data_dir>/arcade/environment_files\fR
and run it locally \(em play does not depend on the server.
.TP
.B online
every move on the official server, counting on the official scorecard.
.TP
.B offline
only games already downloaded \(em no network at all.
.PP
\fBARC_API_KEY\fR unlocks the full remote catalogue; an anonymous key
still lists and downloads the 25 public games. Replays are written to
\fI<data_dir>/arcade/recordings\fR. Her reasoning travels with each
move: the \fBreasoning\fR field of \fBenv.step\fR carries her
\fIwhy\fR onto the official recordings and scorecard.
.SS Her sight \(em games.sight
Boards reach her as cell indices, not pixels \(em the retina is
bypassed, so sight maps each cell through the official 16-colour
palette to RGB, to HSV, to the same V1 \fBname_color\fR her camera
path uses: objects report \fIred(8)\fR, \fIcyan(10)\fR, and a new
board opens with a scene gestalt (\fIscene | dim warm red\fR plus
regional colours) in the same record her episodic memory stores for
camera scenes. Her pointing space covers every parsed object \(em
\fBACTION6\fR clicks land on any cell, so palette swatches and small
sprites are as clickable as the large ones.
.SS The arena \(em games.arena
Local play on \fBpyspiel\fR \(em the same engine the open-sourced Kaggle
Game Arena harness evaluates on. Six games ship as offers:
connect_four, tic_tac_toe, checkers, othello, breakthrough and chess,
each under an \fIarena:<name>\fR id. She plays seat 0; the other seat
is the \fB"random"\fR policy by default or any
\fI(state, player, rng) -> action\fR callable. Observation planes fold
into the int grid her sight renders; one match counts as one "level".
No key and no network are needed \(em the shelf is always open when the
packages are installed.
.SH HER TOOLS
The \fBarcade_*\fR family registered in her tool registry \(em how
she plays. Arguments arrive as strings; each returns a
\fIToolResult\fR (see
.BR genesis-tools (7)).
.TP
.B arcade_directions
Read the directions she is given for the games \(em the rules text
that says she cannot know the instructions and must explore.
.TP
.B arcade_offers
List the games the arcade offers \(em every title on both shelves,
\fIarena:\fR-prefixed and bare.
.TP
.BR arcade_enter " \fI[game_id]\fR"
Go to a game: sit down at \fIgame_id\fR, or let her pick one
herself when no id is given. Opens with her sight's first read of
the board.
.TP
.BR arcade_see " \fI[how]\fR"
Look at the open board: \fItext\fR (the default), \fIimage\fR,
\fIchange\fR, or \fIobjects\fR.
.TP
.BR arcade_act " \fImove\fR"
Make one move in the open game \(em e.g. \fBACTION1\fR, or
\fBACTION6@row,col\fR for a click on a cell. Replies with what
changed and the new state/level.
.TP
.BR arcade_play " \fI[moves]\fR"
Play a bout of the open (or chosen) game \(em a run of moves
(default \fBBOUT_MOVES\fR) rather than a single act.
.TP
.B arcade_leave
Step away from the game \(em the sitting ends; what she remembers
of it is kept.
.TP
.B arcade_status
Report what she remembers of every game \(em the same report
\fB/arcade\fR shows.

.SH INSTALL
.nf
\fBuv sync --extra arc\fR          arc-agi==0.9.9, game-arena, kaggle-environments
\fBuv sync --extra hid\fR          evdev (her uinput hands)
.fi
.PP
arc-agi is pinned at 0.9.9 because 0.9.10 requires Pillow \(>= 13
against the project's pinned 12.3.0.
.BR scripts/install_optional_deps.sh
installs the same packages as wheels and proves the shelf in its
verification pass (\fIarcade games\fR row).
.SH KAGGLE ACCESS
Her Kaggle credential lives at
.IR ~/.kaggle/access_token
(mode 600) \(em a \fBKGAT_\fR token from
.IR "Kaggle \(-> Settings \(-> API" .
The \fBkaggle\fR CLI (2.x) is installed in her environment and picks
it up automatically:
.TP
.B "kaggle competitions submit"
enter open competitions \(em including Kaggle Simulations contests,
which run on the same kaggle-environments stack as the arena.
.TP
.B "kaggle datasets"
download published Game Arena match logs and environment code.
.TP
.B "kaggle benchmarks leaderboard kaggle/game-arena"
pull the arena leaderboards programmatically.
.PP
The official Game Arena leaderboard itself is curated: Kaggle
evaluates invited models, and new entries go through
.IR kaggle-benchmarks@google.com .
An API token does not enrol her \(em her local arena shelf plays the
same games on the same engine regardless.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARC_API_KEY
Official-games key; anonymous access covers the 25 public games.
.TP
.B GENESIS_ARC_MODE
.BR normal " (default), " online ", or " offline .
.TP
.B KAGGLE_API_TOKEN
Alternative to the access_token file for the kaggle CLI.
.SH FILES
.nf
\fIOuter_World/games/arcade.py\fR     the place, memory/chemistry/waves plumbing
