.SH GLOSSARY
.TP
.B arcade
The place in her outer world that offers games \(em offers, not
assignments: she chooses whether to play, and play feeds memory,
emotion, and chemistry like any other act.
.TP
.B shelf / catalogue
One source of games. \fBCombinedGames\fR merges the two shelves
(official ARC-AGI-3 and the local arena) into one offer list;
\fBarena:\fR-prefixed ids route to the arena, bare ids to the
official API.
.TP
.B ARC-AGI-3
The official interactive puzzle benchmark: grid-based levels with
no stated instructions \(em she must explore, remember, and carry
what each level teaches to the next.
.TP
.B arena
The local shelf running on \fBpyspiel\fR \(em the same engine the
Kaggle Game Arena harness evaluates on. Six games, seat 0, a
\fI(state, player, rng) -> action\fR opponent policy.
.TP
.B policy
A callable that picks a move for a seat given the state \(em her
default opponent is the \fB"random"\fR policy.
.TP
.B scorecard
The official server's account of a run \(em reached only in
\fIonline\fR mode; local normal-mode play doesn't count there.
.TP
.B replay / recording
The saved trace of a game under \fI<data_dir>/arcade/recordings\fR
\(em including her \fIreasoning\fR field, the \fIwhy\fR she sent
with each move.
.TP
.B reasoning field
The free-text \fIwhy\fR attached to each \fBenv.step\fR \(em her
thinking travels onto the official recording and scorecard.
.TP
.B gestalt
The scene summary her sight emits when a board opens
.RI ( "scene | dim warm red" " plus regional colors" )
\(em the same record shape her episodic memory stores for camera
scenes.
.TP
.B sight
The mapping from board cells to perception: 16-colour palette
indices through RGB to the V1 \fBname_color\fR vocabulary her
camera path uses \(em boards reach her as colors and objects, not
pixels.
.TP
.B observation planes
The int-grid layers an arena game exposes (pieces, board state)
folded into the grid her sight renders.
.TP
.B level
One playable unit \(em one ARC level, or one arena match.
.TP
.B seat
A player slot in an arena game \(em she plays seat 0.
.TP
.B pyspiel
The OpenSpiel game engine the arena runs on \(em the same stack
Kaggle Simulations contests and the open-sourced harness use.

